            <ArticleTitle>Uterine rupture disguised by urinary retention following a second trimester induced abortion: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s12905-014-0159-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Uterine rupture classically presents with severe abdominal pain, loss of fetal station, vaginal bleeding, and shock.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE PRESENTATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">We present a case of uterine rupture presenting as significant urinary retention that occurred following a second trimester abortion induced with mifepristone and misoprostol. Uterine rupture was discovered unexpectedly on diagnostic laparoscopy. The uterine rupture was contained by dense adhesions between the omentum and bladder with the previous uterine cesarean hysterotomy scar.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This case highlights the difficulties in diagnosis of abnormal placentation and an unusual presentation of uterine rupture. This case was managed successfully laparoscopically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
